    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (69.65) and **Christian Yelich** (69.12) headlining our offensive attack. Despite a challenging matchup against Robbie Ray, **Yordan Alvarez** earns our highest efficiency score of 69.65 due to an elite .473 xwOBA, which effectively mitigates the platoon disadvantage of facing a southpaw. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** offers a high ceiling against Matthews; his strong 69.12 score is bolstered by a favorable platoon split and an opportunity to capitalize on a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher, which maximizes our stolen base potential in this scarcity-driven category. **Kyle Schwarber** (66.09) also remains a core start, anchoring the top of the lineup with the highest leadoff utility score, provided the rain in his matchup holds off.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a score of 48.53. While **Chase Meidroth** offers a valuable blend of leadoff order placement and platoon advantages, his overall efficiency metrics lagged behind **Carson Benge** (58.08) and **Lars Nootbaar** (57.75), whose superior park and skill projections pushed them into the final slots. We are closely monitoring the 33% rain risk affecting **Trea Turner**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Carson Benge**, and **Kyle Schwarber**; should weather force a late-game pivot, we are prepared to utilize our depth. While **Kazuma Okamoto** faces a stiff test against Zack Wheeler with a lower 42.61 score, his inclusion is required to balance our power production, though we will remain vigilant regarding his health and performance throughout the rain-threatened afternoon.",
